   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] [Question] about methylKit",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Jong,<div><br></div><div>MethylKit has multiple annotation functions:</div><div><ul><li>annotate.WithFeature()<br></li><li>annotate.WithFeature.Flank()<br></li><li>annotate.WithGenicParts()<br></li></ul><div>Each of the above performs annotation however to a unique subject. For eg., annotate.WithFeature.Flank() could be used to annotate CpG Islands and shoresl; annotate.WithGenicParts() could be used to annotate genic elements like promoter, introns, exons.</div></div><div><br></div><div>In order to perform annotations, one has to create the subject (ie., CpG islands/shore or genic elements). MethylKit offers functions to create them also.</div><div><br></div><div>One can get very good information about creating and using the annotation objects by following the vignette from the <a href=\"https://code.google.com/p/methylkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://code.google.com/p/methylkit/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234001864000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1j_vOsuOtSSWYpSuZbXvvk\">methylKit website</a>. MethylKit provides very good coersion function that will help you to achieve the kind of table you wanted (Its not straight forward but possible with some knowledge of R/bioconductor and basic linux shell scripting)</div><div><br></div><div>Here is a <a href=\"http://chitka-kalyan.blogspot.fi/2014/10/extending-methylkit-extract-promoters.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://chitka-kalyan.blogspot.fi/2014/10/extending-methylkit-extract-promoters.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234001864000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ucdGrgMORLnvunsrLPFv4\">blog post</a> that may help you reach your goal. I would probably do the following for the kind of table you wanted:</div><div><ol><li>Create annotation object from refseq/ENSEMBL annotation using read.transcript.features()</li><li>Get the DMR object (I am assuming that it will be a methylDiff object) and coerce it into GRanges using as()</li><li>Find intersecting/overlapping ranges  between DMR and each genic region (promoter/exon/intron)</li><li>For each intersecting ranges name an additional column that identifies the genic elements. Eg., label a metacolumn as &#39;promoter&#39; for the promoter overlapping ranges</li><li>combine all the labelled and overlapping ranges into one object eg., c(promoter_DMRs, exon_DMRs........)</li><li>Export the ranges into a bed file/table</li></ol><div>Pls note that the above instructions/functions may not work out of the box. It depends on the kind of the objects one starts with. But I hope this may give you a direction to start with and achieve your table!</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Regards,<br>Kalyan<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"width:auto;height:30px;font-size:0px\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width:auto\"><div style=\"line-height:0\"><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"width:48px;line-height:1;vertical-align:top\" valign=\"top\" align=\"left\"><br></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:8px;font-size:0px\"><br></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:auto;height:48px;line-height:1;padding:0px;vertical-align:middle\" valign=\"middle\" align=\"left\"><br></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tbody>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</table>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t</div></td></tr>\r\n\t\t\t<tr><td style=\"width:auto;height:20px;font-size:0px\"> </td></tr>\r\n\t\t</tbody>\r\n\t</table>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<br></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
